# scripts/security/external-agents.local
#
# User LaunchAgents deliberately managed outside this flake. The security
# audit verifies these records and the re-registration helper only operates
# on rows explicitly marked relaunch=true.
#
# Each data row has exactly seven `|`-separated fields:
# Label|owner-repo-root|source-plist|deployed-plist|ProgramArguments[0]|enabled-or-disabled|true-or-false
# Label is the exact extensionless launchd Label. Paths are absolute and
# canonical; source-plist must be `<owner-repo-root>/.../<Label>.plist`.
# The deployed path is `$HOME/Library/LaunchAgents/<Label>.plist` when enabled
# and `<Label>.plist.disabled` when disabled. Source and deployed plist files
# must be regular files, byte-identical, and agree with Label and
# ProgramArguments[0]. Pipes, carriage returns, and newlines are not allowed
# in values.
#
# A row is the local inventory for one externally owned job, independent of
# whether it is eligible for a Nushell-path relaunch. Use `false` for shell or
# other jobs that do not need that re-registration. Disabled rows cannot be
# relaunch-enabled. Unknown on-disk or loaded jobs under the configured prefix
# remain WARN, make `just security-audit --strict` fail, and block relaunch
# before any job is changed.
#
# Optional relaunch directives are comments with the following exact forms:
# relaunch-prefix=com.example.
# relaunch-lock-path=/absolute/path/to/shared.lock
# relaunch-lock-label=com.example.import
# relaunch-lock-label=com.example.verify
# These directives are parsed as data; the file is never sourced as shell.
#
# Copy to scripts/security/external-agents.local (gitignored) and edit.
#
# relaunch-prefix=com.example.
# relaunch-lock-path=/path/to/shared.lock
# relaunch-lock-label=com.example.import
# com.example.daily-thing|/var/example-user/repos/daily-thing|/var/example-user/repos/daily-thing/launchd/com.example.daily-thing.plist|/var/example-user/Library/LaunchAgents/com.example.daily-thing.plist|/var/example-user/repos/daily-thing/bin/daily-thing|enabled|true
# com.example.shell-monitor|/var/example-user/repos/monitor|/var/example-user/repos/monitor/launchd/com.example.shell-monitor.plist|/var/example-user/Library/LaunchAgents/com.example.shell-monitor.plist|/var/example-user/repos/monitor/check.sh|enabled|false
